# WP Milestone 3 pursuit corpus for physics.kinematics.catch-up.equal-position. Each case names its
# construction and kind. Offsets are byte ranges of the text, computed apart from the reader.
case depart-later
family physics.kinematics.catch-up.equal-position
construction a later departure from the same place
kind positive
text A car leaves a town at 20 m/s. A truck leaves the same town 10 s later at 30 m/s. When does the truck catch up with the car?
expect outcome interpreted
expect body car from "car" at 2..5
expect body truck from "truck" at 33..38
expect event depart-car from "leaves" at 6..12
expect event depart-truck from "leaves" at 39..45
expect event meeting from "catch up" at 102..110
expect given car initial_velocity 20 m/s from "20 m/s" at 23..29 by speed-of-subject
expect given truck start_time 10 s from "10 s" at 60..64 by later
expect given truck initial_velocity 30 m/s from "30 m/s" at 74..80 by speed-of-subject
expect inferred q-start_time-car 0 s by clock-origin
expect stated q-start_position-car 0 m by same-place
expect stated q-start_position-truck 0 m by same-place
expect inferred assumption both bodies move the same way along one line
expect goal meeting_time from "When" at 82..86
end
case pronoun
