end
case head-start
family physics.kinematics.catch-up.equal-position
construction a head start ahead of the other body, same direction stated
kind positive
text A cyclist rides at 5 m/s, 100 m ahead of a runner. The runner runs at 7 m/s in the same direction. How long until the runner catches the cyclist?
expect outcome interpreted
expect body cyclist from "cyclist" at 2..9
expect body runner from "runner" at 43..49
expect event meeting from "catches" at 125..132
expect given cyclist initial_velocity 5 m/s from "5 m/s" at 19..24 by speed-of-subject
expect given cyclist start_position 100 m from "100 m" at 26..31 by ahead
expect inferred runner start_position 0 m by origin-at-reference
expect given runner initial_velocity 7 m/s from "7 m/s" at 70..75 by speed-of-subject
expect inferred q-start_time-cyclist 0 s by same-start-time
expect inferred q-start_time-runner 0 s by same-start-time
expect stated assumption both bodies move the same way along one line from "same direction"
expect goal meeting_time from "How long" at 99..107
end
case ambiguous-it
family physics.kinematics.catch-up.equal-position
construction "It" after a sentence naming both bodies
kind ambiguous
text A car leaves a town at 20 m/s. A truck follows the car 10 s later. It drives at 30 m/s. When does the truck catch up?
expect outcome needs clarification: 1 to settle
expect body car from "car" at 2..5
expect body truck from "truck" at 33..38
expect event depart-car from "leaves" at 6..12
expect event meeting from "catch up" at 108..116
expect given car initial_velocity 20 m/s from "20 m/s" at 23..29 by speed-of-subject
expect given truck start_time 10 s from "10 s" at 55..59 by later
expect given c1 initial_velocity 30 m/s from "30 m/s" at 80..86 by speed-of-subject
expect goal meeting_time from "When" at 88..92
expect clarify c1 does "It" at 67..69 mean the truck or the car?
end
